WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.260
In closing,

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.530
I pray for your health and success, dear sisters,

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.410
and thus, I bid you farewell.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.850
Representing the remaining student body,
I am Ogasawara Sachiko.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.150
What's the matter, Yumi?

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.880
Was there something wrong with it?

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:29.680
No...

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.030
Thinking about how the graduation
ceremony is really today...

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.690
...has made me nervous somehow.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.690
So the Lady Roses will really be gone.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.070
Yes...

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.500
It's kind of hard to believe, though...

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.510
Come, let's all get to our classrooms soon, too.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.380
Everyone, thank you for being here
for my farewell speech rehearsal.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.220
Today, the Lady Roses will
be graduating from Lillian.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.180
I wonder what thoughts are
going through their minds.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.630
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:15.400
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.200
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.080
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.540
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.880
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:35.420
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:48.330
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:57.580
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:04.480
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:11.960
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:19.620
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:27.110
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:34.580
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:42.680
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:50.200
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:57.130
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:05.140
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.880
The Years That Flew By

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.950
Year 3, Camellia Class

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.950
We congratulate you on this day.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.920
We will now come around to
pin these flowers on you.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:21.760
To Our Upperclassmen of Year 3,
Camellia Class Congratulations on Graduating

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.530
To Our Upperclassmen of Year 3,
Camellia Class Congratulations on Graduating
We will wholeheartedly devote
ourselves to this endeavor,

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.190
To Our Upperclassmen of Year 3,
Camellia Class Congratulations on Graduating
but considering that this
is a task we are unused to,

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.400
we ask for your forgiveness
for any mistake we may make.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.170
Congratulations.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:30.840
Congratulations.
Congratulations.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:31.770
Congratulations.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:32.940
Congratulations.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.010
Congratulations.
Congratulations.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.970
Congratulations.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.440
But why is it that none of this feels real?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.010
Rosa Chinensis.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.810
Congratulations.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:54.990
What's wrong?

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.500
P-Pardon me.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.930
She has long been a fan
of yours, Rosa Chinensis.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.300
I see. Thank you.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:12.180
Oh, yes. We have a student
absent due to the flu today.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.480
If it would be all right,
I'll take her flower to her.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.420
P-Please do, Rosa Chinensis.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:21.290
Thank you very much, Rosa Chinensis.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.920
Good grief.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.150
I'm being a total busybody
right up to the end, aren't I?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.990
Even though today is the graduation ceremony.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.340
But this graduation ceremony thing...

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.410
It's a ceremony conducted for the
purpose of presenting diplomas.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:49.480
Is there a need for something
this elaborate just to do that?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.510
This is bad.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.320
Up until yesterday, I was steeped in
sentimentality in my own way, but...

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.390
For goodness sake, today is
the graduation ceremony...

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:10.340
But maybe graduation ceremonies
are held for the family members.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.040
And he said he'd come, too...

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.850
I wonder what Yamanobe-san is doing?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:25.420
Here.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:25.650
And what's Yoko being so
considerate for, right up to the end?
Here.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.720
And what's Yoko being so
considerate for, right up to the end?

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.690
And what's Yoko being so
considerate for, right up to the end?
Thank you.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:28.680
And what's Yoko being so
considerate for, right up to the end?

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.520
And over there, she has no sense of tension.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.260
I guess I'm the same.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:40.300
For goodness sake, today is
the graduation ceremony...

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.080
Are you an American?

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.280
I got it! You're half-American!

00:05:59.420 --> 00:05:59.690
Lillian
Kindergarten

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:00.360
Lillian
Kindergarten
I'm not...

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:00.490
Lillian
Kindergarten

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.460
Lillian
Kindergarten
Say, is your dad an American? Or is it...

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:03.790
Lillian
Kindergarten

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.360
You're running away?

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.020
Go away, you big forehead!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:20.710
Now, Eriko, stop this.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:21.210
Stop this.
Now, Eriko, stop this.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:21.680
Stop this.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.040
Sato Sei.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.310
Yes, Sir.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:50.800
Sato-san.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.710
Have you decided what club
you are going to join?

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.140
If you are interested,
let us go observe some clubs together.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.810
Since we are in the same group anyway.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.110
Outside middle school applicant, huh?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:05.310
What?

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:10.350
I haven't been called "Sato-san"
by a classmate in ages.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.450
It was refreshing, that's all...

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:13.960
...Yoko-san.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.000
Thank you for letting me know, Sei-san.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.670
You are welcome.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.510
It isn't written in the
student handbook, you know.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.810
That students at Lillian don't
address each other by last name,

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.470
but by their first names.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:40.710
So you approached me because you
don't fit in around here, either?

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.420
It was because I found
myself interested somehow...

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:46.450
...in you.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.050
I see.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.660
So, you're a meddlesome busybody.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.140
Since then, who knows how
many arguments we had...

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.870
...because of the unwanted remarks I offered.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.070
But even that is over as of today.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.940
Diploma
Sei Sato

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.890
Mizuno Yoko.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.010
Yes, Sir.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:25.260
The first time I saw Yoko was during
the middle school entrance ceremony.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:31.500
Representing the incoming class,
Year 1, Plum Class, Mizuno Yoko.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:32.560
Yes, Sir.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.210
She's an outside applicant,

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.650
and yet, she's giving the speech as
the incoming class representative.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.350
She must be a really excellent student.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:51.120
I didn't want to compete with
a model student like that,

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.550
so I didn't really want to get to know her, but...

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.060
Eriko-san, your ribbon is tied so beautifully.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:03.330
You think so?

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.040
Do you have a trick to it?

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.250
If you don't mind, would
you teach me how you tie it?

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:22.690
All right.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.960
There's no trick to it,

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.740
but if you tug on both sides at the end,

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.170
it can feel invigorating.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.130
I'll practice that.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:42.140
Though I may never get as good as you.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:47.670
A model student, who doesn't
hide how she works hard, huh?

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.710
Unlike me, since I only devoted myself
to the things that interested me.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.420
It was then that I started thinking
Yoko was interesting.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:01.760
But neither Yoko nor I will
ever tie these scarves again.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.600
Graduation
Ceremony

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.730
Graduation
Ceremony
Farewell speech.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.370
Graduation
Ceremony
Representing the remaining student body,

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.130
Graduation
Ceremony
Year 2, Pine Class, Ogasawara Sachiko.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.970
To our dear sisters,

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.640
taking wing from the high school
division of Lillian Girls' Academy.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:27.150
Congratulations on graduating...

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.580
Sachiko...

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.160
I want to go to you right this minute.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.430
But if I go now,

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:11.830
people will come to think you can't
do anything without your big sister.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.990
You are the next Rosa Chinensis.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:16.870
Please, pull yourself together somehow.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:29.020
It's too much! I can't watch anymore!

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.260
As representative of the remaining student body,

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.390
I wish you the best from the bottom of my heart.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:48.400
Thank you very much for all the
guidance you have offered to us.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:53.670
You have carefully guarded the
tradition of Lillian Girls' Academy...

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:54.810
...and from now on,

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.900
it is my intention that we will
carry on that tradition, without fail.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.410
In closing,

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:12.790
I pray for your health and success, dear sisters,

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.160
and thus, I bid you farewell.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.360
Representing the remaining student body,
I am Ogasawara Sachiko.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.030
And...

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:22.860
Hasekura Rei.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:42.740
Is the farewell speech normally
supposed to garner such applause?

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:46.190
The valedictory speech.

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:47.730
Representing the graduating students,

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.790
Year 3, Camellia Class, Mizuno Yoko.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.890
Good grief, this is going to be tough.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.670
After that performance just now,

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.470
I can't break down in tears and
become unable to finish the speech,

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:01.170
even if it kills me.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.780
I'll just have to be every bit the model student...

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:07.580
...and get this graduation ceremony
back onto an orderly track.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:10.640
But if...

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.020
...I find myself in a situation like Sachiko's,

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.090
would those two do what Rei did for her?

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.930
Never mind leaping to my aid,

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.800
they would throw their heads back and laugh.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:38.410
I feel bad about this...

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.240
Did you just get here?

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.410
No, well...

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.710
The graduation ceremony is over already.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.350
Yes, and I feel bad about that.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:59.330
So you were mistaken for a suspicious person.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:01.030
Well, uh...

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:04.810
But it's true that I'm not family or anything,

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.770
so I have no right to be at
the graduation ceremony...

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:07.930
That's ridiculous.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:12.440
I am graduating and I wanted you to come,

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.580
so that gives you plenty of right.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.010
I see, you're exactly right.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.020
You should go soon.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.220
Yes.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:30.760
Thank you for coming.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.020
It was nothing.

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:35.430
Eriko-san.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.530
Congratulations on graduating.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.350
The beginning was boring,

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.510
but it got interesting towards the end.

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:56.280
Really, you were so cool, Rei-chan.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.620
Pardon me, thank you for waiting.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.560
Now, where shall we take the photos?

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.800
Onee-sama, may I have a moment?

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.700
Onee-sama, here.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.200
You will feel better if you blow your nose.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:17.640
You know...

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.440
Whether it is dry eye or hay fever
or whatever, you will feel better.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.090
I was in a similar situation as
you the day before yesterday...

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:29.210
...and I received a tissue
from Shimako-san and...

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:31.850
This will really make me feel better?

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:39.320
Come to think of it, where's Shimako?

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.130
Shizuka-sama?

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.940
The Yamayuri Council is going
to be taking pictures now.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.720
If you are willing, please join us.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:04.380
Because I, too, will be leaving Lillian in March?

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:09.260
Thank you, but I will decline this invitation.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.190
But...

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:12.830
Shimako.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.500
Oh, you're here too, Shizuka?

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.360
Congratulations on graduating.

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:24.510
I will not say farewell,

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.880
for I believe we will meet again someday.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.580
I agree. Let's meet again.

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:32.480
Good day.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:47.960
Say...

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:49.030
Huh?

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.170
We once had a huge fight, remember?

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:53.700
Oh...

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.580
What was the fight about again?

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.480
What? You're kidding. You've forgotten?

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:03.350
I have this vague feeling that I said
something that offended you...

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:05.580
...or you said something like that to me, but...

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:10.980
You called me an American,
so I called you big forehead.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:12.660
Oh my.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:17.060
I guess these are things
that tend to get forgotten.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:36.350
We look up to the invaluable boon
our mentors have bestowed upon us...

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:49.990
It has already been many years
in this garden of learning...

00:17:50.700 --> 00:18:04.100
Looking back, how quickly these
months and years have passed.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:19.760
Now, it is time to part, to say farewell.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:33.830
The friendship we shared,
so much to be thankful for every day...

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:47.650
Even after we have parted, do not thee forget.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:19:01.400
Find success, make thy mark,
devote thee to thine endeavors.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:16.980
Now, it is time to part, to say farewell.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.010
I will send you the photos.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.750
Thank you. I look forward to seeing them.

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:26.320
Um...

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:30.750
I will also send you the Lillian Ledger's
commemorative graduation issue.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.630
That'll be something to look
forward to in a different sense.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.530
Lady Roses, um...

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:40.260
I am very sorry to have
troubled you in various ways.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:45.110
But I was really happy to have had the
privilege of attending high school...

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:48.170
...during the same time as you...

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:49.840
Oh? What?

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:53.840
I can't believe myself. I can't... I'm sorry!

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.850
I apologize that things have
been like this to the very end.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:04.960
I am sure it may be worrisome
that our chief editor is like that,

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.930
but we at the school paper will work as one...

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.590
...to put out a great issue to send to you,

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.960
so please forgive her for today.

00:21:15.970 --> 00:21:19.030
There doesn't seem to be anything
we need to be worried about.

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:19.760
I agree.

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:23.300
Shall we get going soon?

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:38.590
See you.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:41.920
See you.

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:45.220
See you.

00:21:53.940 --> 00:21:57.210
There may have still been a lot
of things that were left unsaid.

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.610
But right now, we have just one wish.

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:04.580
May you be happy. May you all,
every last one of you, be happy.

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:10.960
To have been at this school...

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:12.860
...and had the privilege of meeting you all...

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:15.160
For that, I am glad.

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:30.770
Onee-sama, in helping my mother
yesterday, I made pot stickers.

